    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1832 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-of-greece">Otto of Bavaria</a> as king, it was the first nation state carved from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</li><li>Pursuing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/megali-idea">Great Idea</a> of uniting all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>, it more than doubled its territory before defeat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> in 1922.</li><li>Abolished in 1924, restored in 1935, it lived through occupation, civil war and a military junta that ended the monarchy in 1973.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-of-greece">Alexander of Greece</a> died in October 1920 of an infection from a bite by a pet monkey; his death led to the return of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a> and changed the course of the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

